 @beingcensoredbyYT  Thanks for the reply. Looks like we have some disagreement but I enjoyed reading your response. On point 4, I say raise taxes only because we cannot continue this running spending deficits year after year. Now if we could reduce the government budget so that current or our proposed tax revenues would cover government spending, I am open to discussing that for sure. Also I am not fundamentally opposed to tariffs when we have to deal with countries who unfairly target our products. I think we can find common ground on that. 

I am going to have to think about your objections to point 5 as I have a problem with the idea that most wealthy people actually contributed to the economy. I say that because I am aware of way to many situations where the wealthy have merely gamed the system to their advantage without adding any real value to our country. Stock buybacks with excess profits to enhance stock value for corporate executives would be one example of that. I alluded to that in my point 7. Let me think about the rest of your response to point 5 some more.

Again thanks for your well thought out reply. Enjoy the upcoming holidays.

